WEBVTT

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.130
It's been a long time since I've done that...

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.940
Monday!

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:25.720
No way!

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.550
I haven't sent it, have I?

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.310
I didn't e-mail Tomoya, did I?

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:32.850
Quick!

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.930
I'll have to send it quick...

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:39.820
Tomoya?

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:45.820
Stop-

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:18.430
Yo, Tomoya-kun.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:19.790
Sorry I took so long.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.800
Wait a moment, Iori.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.170
This is Enaka-san,

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.900
who takes care of our circle's taxes.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:30.520
Ah, hello, I am Aki.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.300
I mean, what in the world is this about?!

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.500
Tomoya-kun, when you called me,

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.060
I was in a meeting with Enaka-san concerning store deals.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.540
Once I told her about your situation,

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:43.110
she said she'd bring the car!

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.590
That's not good!

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:48.150
I only asked to borrow money for the travel expenses, anyway.

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:51.770
Taking a train and taxi will take a long time.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:54.940
And what if you miss the last train?

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:59.240
Come on, let's go, Tomoya-kun,

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.630
to Nasu Highlands.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.500
I see, she's all alone at the villa,

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:09.240
and suddenly got sick, huh?

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:13.340
Both her parents are back in England,

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:15.650
and there's nobody who can go check on her,

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.230
so I'm going instead.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.600
So, what about your development deadline?

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.920
Can you make the print shop's deadline?

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:26.590
I can't worry about such things now.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.480
My friend is sick.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:34.610
Saying things like that is not very much like you.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:39.700
I'm not as clever, composed,

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:42.330
or indeed heartless as you.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:48.840
And that is exactly why you've come this far, exhibiting last-minute power I'd never have expected.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:49.800
What?

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:54.470
I've heard it's a major work with a scenario of over two megabytes, more than thirty music tracks,

00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:59.790
and better than 100 event illustrations once the art is done.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:00.760
Your game.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.150
We just... ended up getting more of everything.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:07.170
Normally, that'd lead to setbacks in an instant.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.190
How did you push everybody forward?

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:13.570
What is a high schoolers' play circle doing?

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:15.330
It's not play...

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.460
That's right.

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:19.270
You've always been unbelievably serious.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:22.330
But what about this time?

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:27.710
Tomoya-kun, you are in no position to head for Nasu Highlands now.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.160
You should have left this to somebody else,

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.130
and not leave your house before the development deadline.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:39.140
I can't so selfishly and conveniently leave something like that to the other members.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.360
Is that really all?

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.590
What do you mean?

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:55.600
As for me, Tomoya-kun,

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:01.240
I can only think that you seem to want to keep
Kashiwagi Eri- no, Sawamura Eriri, all for yourself.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:01.740
Tha-

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:35.010
Eriri!

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:36.260
Hey, Eriri!

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.070
Iori, help me!

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:41.150
S-Sure.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.700
Let's carry her to the bedroom!

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:53.290
Enaka-san, please bring the luggage in from the car.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:06.050
Okay, we're going now.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:07.740
Thank you so much.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:08.780
What?

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.850
We help each other in times of trouble.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:14.840
I contacted a shop we use.

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:18.750
They said they can wait until noon today, but no more.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:19.360
Huh?

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.690
Contact your friends in Tokyo right away,

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.520
and make the final version.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:25.070
You have half a day.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:26.680
You can just about make it, can't you?

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:29.960
Sorry, Iori.

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:32.050
It's fine, really.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:36.420
If you can solve it with money and diplomacy, it's not a huge effort.

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:37.630
See ya!

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:55.150
So, what did the doctor say?

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:58.200
Apparently you may even have the flu,

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:00.420
so you'll have to rest for now.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.940
That's the worst.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:04.760
I haven't caught a cold in a while, either.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:06.910
You used to go to bed to rest right away.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:11.630
For Hinamatsuri, Shichi-Go-San and Christmas, too.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:12.960
Shut up.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.770
By the way, my pictures.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.360
Yeah, I saw them.

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:22.260
So, how were they?

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:25.590
Yeah, all seven were fine.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:28.340
R-Really?

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:29.880
That's great!

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:33.190
So, you're done with all your work now.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.900
So sleep a bit more.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:36.690
Yeah!

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.590
So, did you finish the game?

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:43.200
You being here means that it's okay, right?

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:48.580
You added my pictures to the game,
debugged it, and sent it for printing, right?

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:52.330
I finished the illustrations!

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:56.080
So you finished the game, right?

00:07:58.140 --> 00:07:59.990
What are you doing?!

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:02.700
What are you doing, Tomoya?!

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:06.370
Don't push yourself too hard!

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:07.230
Come o-

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.970
Stop idling here and go work right away!

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:16.810
Wasn't working hard without giving up until the very last moment one of your few good points?!

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:19.600
Someone suddenly falling ill and the development deadline...

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.440
Isn't it obvious which you'd pick?

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:23.970
Of course you'd pick both!

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:24.950
It's too late now.

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.200
Do you want to waste my week?

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:30.660
Do you want to waste all of our half a year?

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:33.580
It just means that the packaged version won't make it to winter Comiket.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.250
It's pretty much done already.

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:37.900
It doesn't matter when we release it.

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:39.750
What are you saying, Tomoya?

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:41.350
Hey?

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:45.420
<i>It really is nothing but contradictory.</i>

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.510
Stupid, stupid!

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:50.940
Tomoya, you big idiot!

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:52.250
You're right.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:00.620
I'm sorry, Tomo-kun...

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:03.530
I couldn't keep our promise...

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:06.530
I'm sorry...

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:11.530
<i>Because there's no way I can neglect her.</i>

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:18.250
Cheer up and eat something.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:23.590
The value of this game won't fade just from being a little late.

00:09:23.590 --> 00:09:26.890
Also, we'll be able to release at winter Comiket.

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:29.290
A hundred home-burned ones, anyway.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:34.950
But that's not enough to beat rouge en rouge... to beat Hashima Izumi.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:37.180
Forget about that fight already.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:43.060
But I can't become your number one then.

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:46.680
There's no way that's true.

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:47.190
What?

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:49.910
These are amazing.

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:53.030
They're the best pictures I've seen all year.

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:57.540
I felt chills when I came here and first saw these pictures.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.690
They're realistic but moe,

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:01.420
beautiful but cute,

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:05.620
amazing pictures, unlike anything I've seen before.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:10.050
S-So, can I ask again?

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:19.230
Are my pictures more amazing than hers?

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:20.410
Yes.

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:24.280
Better than hers, or any other illustrator's?

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:25.070
Yes.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:29.570
I became your number one!

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:31.820
Yes!

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:35.890
I see, I won!

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:41.900
Hashima Izumi, Hyoudou Michiru, and Kasumigaoka Utaha...

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.080
I beat all of them!

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:47.550
I didn't say that much, stupid.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:50.310
Come on, your rice gruel.

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:52.850
I'd prefer cup yakisoba!

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:54.100
Hey!

00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:59.020
Hey, which present?

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:00.350
Tomoya, you pick!

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:03.770
You should just pick it yourself.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:07.480
But it's the one and only Christmas present.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:09.280
W-Well...

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:13.030
It's a good chance, so I'll pick this red brooch.

00:11:13.030 --> 00:11:14.970
<i>This is for you.</i>

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:17.490
What? Pick the ring!

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:20.120
That's how you can hear Celvis' proposal!

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:24.770
Celvis really is more cringy than I thought, going for the Christmas proposal.

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:25.430
What?

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:28.630
I won't forgive anybody who disses Celvis, not even you, Tomoya!

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:31.340
What are you doing?

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:38.880
Even so, we're still the same as back then, aren't we?

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:39.810
Well, yeah.

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:42.920
From morning to evening, without even stepping foot outside,

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:45.690
watching anime and playing games...

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:48.220
Because you're sick.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:50.100
Back then, and even now.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:50.690
You're right.

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:53.450
<i>I have something important to tell you.</i>

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:59.110
But let's go back tomorrow.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:01.060
Will your health be good enough?

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:01.930
Yeah.

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:04.410
I'll have the driver come pick us up.

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:06.940
So let's go home together.

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:07.920
I see.

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:12.810
Once we're back, I'll apologise to everybody.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:16.410
That I'm sorry that we couldn't make the deadline.

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:17.610
I'll apologise.

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:19.060
I'm the circle representative, after all.

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:21.140
No, let me apologise.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.690
But I was the one who gave up in the end-

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:24.640
Tomoya.

00:12:26.130 --> 00:12:28.520
I want to apologise.

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:29.640
Eriri...

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:33.650
Because failing to meet the deadline due to my obsessing over quality...

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:38.130
...is my fault, my responsibility,

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:40.660
and my pride.

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:43.560
You too, Tomoya. I'm sorry.

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:49.040
<i>I'll become your number one.</i>

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:52.050
<i>Until then, I'll never apologise.</i>

00:12:54.650 --> 00:12:55.970
I'm sorry.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:57.670
Yeah.

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:04.770
Hurry, everybody!

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:06.730
I'll go do a round of greetings before the doors open,

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:08.730
so let's finish our preparations quickly!

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:13.750
In the end, we ended up being busy until the very last moment, like with every event.

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:15.880
We were supposed to have plenty of time.

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:18.250
If we hadn't released a trial version right beforehand,

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:20.610
added 4-koma manga to the manual,

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:24.210
or added bonus content to the game, that is.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:29.420
B-But if you have extra time, doesn't it feel natural to add something extra?

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:30.570
T-That's right!

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:33.590
For a doujin game, lame inside jokes are absolutely necessary!

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:33.880
Yeah, yeah!

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:38.220
Well, everybody seems to have been busy, so that's nice.

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:42.970
But compared to that, I've been just a bit bored.

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:46.070
That can't be helped, Hyoudou-san.

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:47.850
We have a spot along the wall.

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:54.020
Normally, this spot should be taken by a big-shot circle which prepares to sell four-digit numbers.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:59.280
It is way too much for a small to medium circle trying to sneakily sell a hundred home-burned copies-

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:01.210
Sorry I missed the deadline!

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:05.040
I apologised properly, but you just keep complaining!

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.950
What you just said was pretty much the same,

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:12.460
but I've never heard such an arrogant apology before.

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:13.720
You're right!

00:14:13.720 --> 00:14:15.150
I thought she apologised,

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:17.140
but it ended up being nothing but bragging.

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:19.920
That's how confident I am with my future work!

00:14:20.260 --> 00:14:23.230
The final seven illustrations in particular are all-time top artworks...

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:25.940
...worthy of being part of Kashiwagi Eri's brilliant works collection-

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:29.180
We got it already, so don't get too carried away, it's not a pretty sight.

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:33.440
But you know, Tomoya...

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:36.610
Eriri is not at fault for anything.

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:42.580
Eriri did her very best for this game and the circle.

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:43.780
We all know that.

00:14:44.470 --> 00:14:50.190
Also, when the circle fails, all members together have to take responsibility for it.

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:51.070
Right?

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:52.020
Well,

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:54.280
that she did her very best,

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:56.470
and that they are all-time top artworks,

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:57.880
is impossible to deny.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:59.240
Really.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.550
How did she draw these?

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:04.460
Megumi, I'm really sorry.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:10.020
I don't know how to feel about you only apologising to me,
the one who said you don't need to apologise.

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:13.290
But Katou, you worked really hard too.

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:15.400
Enough about that already.

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:17.870
You two are okay with that, right?

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:30.510
Iori!

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.920
Huh, Tomoya-kun?

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:37.540
Taking the trouble to come to the space where your nemesis is at?

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.120
What wind blew you here?

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:43.160
You know, you were so kind just a while back,

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:45.240
so there's no need to play the baddie now either, is there?

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:47.640
Apparently you were a lot of help.

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:50.650
I can't remember because I was asleep,

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:54.140
but I'm really sorry about everything, Hashima.

00:15:56.150 --> 00:15:59.170
Hey, stop treating me like I'm a good guy!

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:02.160
I have a reputation within my circle to hold up!

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:04.530
What in the world are you fighting against?

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:05.780
Huh?

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:09.210
This winter Comiket,

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:13.250
I and Blessing Software completely lose!

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:14.570
H-Hey!

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:15.780
Sawamura-senpai!

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:18.060
I mean, Kashiwagi-sensei!

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:18.800
That's...

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:20.250
No, let me apologise.

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:25.010
Because I can't move forward if I don't admit losing here.

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:28.940
I was scared of you.

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:31.210
No, I still am.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:33.020
Scared of me?

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:37.020
You closed up to me with such vigour, and surpassed me in such short time,

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:42.240
that I was afraid you'd eventually be so far above me that I wouldn't even realise I'd been surpassed.

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:42.800
Huh?

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:43.580
W-Wait-

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:47.030
So I did and said mean things to you.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:51.000
I am truly sorry.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:54.790
Well, there are other things too...

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:57.500
But...

00:16:57.500 --> 00:16:59.360
I won't lose next time!

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.790
Sawamura-senpai...

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:03.050
If you've improved,

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:05.550
I'll just have to improve even more!

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.800
And now I can do it!

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:14.860
So, until the next event.

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:15.630
Yes!

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:16.560
I'll be waiting!

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:19.600
I'll take on your challenge any time!

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.060
Bring it on!

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:23.080
What's with that arrogant attitude?

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:25.700
So high and mighty!

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:26.650
I'm sorry!

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:30.110
It seems they managed to make up.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:32.130
That's great!

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:36.130
That's not something the one who
agitated them the most should say.

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:37.540
Well, be that as it may,

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:41.470
is it okay for you to hang out here, Tomoya-kun?

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:42.130
Huh?

00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:46.380
Your circle has become a hot topic!

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:51.640
Did you not check what people thought about the trial edition you released?

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:57.530
There's been a lot of hype ever since Kashiwagi Eri and Kasumi Utako were singled out.

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:00.670
Eriri!

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:02.300
No running!

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:12.570
I'm borrowing that, Iori.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:13.980
Akane-san...

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:15.220
Akane-san?

00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:16.790
So you were here, Kousaka-san?

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:19.810
It's been a while since you've come to an event!

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:23.290
I found something interesting this time.

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:35.220
What's that?

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:36.510
Ah!

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.810
Finally you're back!

00:18:39.330 --> 00:18:40.810
Hey, Tomo!

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:43.900
What should we do about this?!

00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:51.650
<i>And so, the first winter Comiket for us, Blessing Software,</i>

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:57.890
<i>was over in under thirty minutes.</i>

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:05.800
Hey!

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:07.460
Quick, everybody!

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:08.470
So sluggish...

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:10.960
I really can't handle crowds.

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:17.560
Should I take that?

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:21.720
It's fine.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:23.020
I see.

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:24.770
It's over.

00:19:24.770 --> 00:19:26.460
It went so fast.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:29.280
I'm sorry.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:31.200
I said so earlier, too.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.830
It's nobody's fault.

00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:38.110
Ah, Katou, straight from there.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:40.370
We're going to our after-party.

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:45.370
I'll go home today.

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:47.290
Wha-

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.970
So this way.

00:19:48.970 --> 00:19:50.560
See you, Aki-kun.

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:52.430
Ah, but,

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:54.520
we'll just eat a little, and go home right away.

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:56.720
Even so, I'm not coming today.

00:19:57.230 --> 00:20:01.460
It's because we didn't have a completed version at winter Comiket, after all?

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:02.730
You were annoyed, right?

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:05.620
I'm truly sorry, Katou...

00:20:07.460 --> 00:20:08.480
But I...

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:15.280
You're so wrong, Aki-kun.

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:16.630
Katou...

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:24.540
Why didn't you speak with me?

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:28.030
About the deadline and about Eriri?

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:30.540
About giving up on winter Comiket?

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:34.350
Why didn't you say anything?

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:39.010
I thought I chose the same thing as you.

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:42.130
I didn't object to anything.

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:43.770
I wouldn't have.

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:48.270
But even so, you said nothing to me.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:51.270
You took all the burden upon yourself.

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:54.320
<i>I'm free the whole weekend, so if necessary...</i>

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:57.910
<i>...contact me right away. I'll even rush to Nasu Highlands.</i>

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:02.410
I think you did the right thing.

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:04.840
But I can't accept it.

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:07.300
I can't fully deal with it yet.

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:10.920
<i>Katou wasn't crying.</i>

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:13.750
<i>However, that's exactly why...</i>

00:21:14.530 --> 00:21:17.060
<i>...seeing that new emotion in her...</i>

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:20.800
<i>...hurt so much I couldn't believe it.</i>
